From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Count a pairing file another app put in place

iloader writes the pairing file of a LiveContainer+SideStore into the
built-in SideStore's Documents as ALTPairingFile.mobiledevicepairing,
and Cartouche's setup does the same with the file iloader exports. The
boot sequence reads it (fetchPairingFile tries each name), but
hasPairingFile counted only a file under the protocol SideStore had
recorded itself, so the onboarding asked for a pairing file it already
had. It now counts any file that fetchPairingFile reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJorvBGmBB88WUcRVhE7
---
 SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift b/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
--- a/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
+++ b/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
@@ -65,7 +65,11 @@
         if let mode = persistedActiveProtocol, hasPairingFile(for: mode) {
             return true
         }
-        return false
+        // A pairing file another app put in place has no protocol recorded
+        // yet: iloader writes one for a LiveContainer+SideStore, and Cartouche
+        // from its setup. The boot sequence reads it (fetchPairingFile), so
+        // count it too.
+        return fetchPairingFile() != nil
     }
 
     nonisolated func metadata(for mode: PairingProtocol) -> PairingFileMetadata {
